This is a valid solution, but it only provides connectivity to the vax's that 
add TCP/IP  (never-mind the problem of TCP/IP for out non-VMS system).  This
currently would not be possible for many reasons ($$$, politics, etc). 
Therefore it seems a gateway of some form would be best?
	Here are the products that I have found thus far:
		1 DECServer 700
		2 Coefficient's MGATE
		3 Novell's Netware for LAT
		4 Interconnections TES
		5 Interconnections Leverage Gateway
		6 Pathworks

1. The Decserver 700 will not convert TCP/IP to LAT, but you can tie two ports
together to form a pseudo-gateway.

2. MGATE provides IPX/SPX to LAT gateway services.  It requires a TSR be run on
the PC.  It uses the INT 14 facility so almost any emulator should work.

3. Netware for LAT will convert TCP/IP to LAT and convert IPX/SPX to LAT.  I
have seen this product and it does work.  However I would need to upgrade all my
copies of Smarterm to get the N for L support.

4. TES adds the IPX/SPX protocol to the VAX.  This has the same drawback as
adding TCP/IP to the VAX.

5. Leverage Gateway ???

6. Pathworks seems like overkill.


Any others?  Does anyone have experience with any of these products?  Any other
advice??

