.TH SIZEDRIVE 8 "22 March 1994"
.SH NAME
sizedrive \- query SCSI disk for geometry information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sizedrive
.I drive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Sizedrive
is a program which queries a SCSI disk drive to determine what its geometry
parameters might be.
.I Drive
can be any of rzNN, rzNN[letter], rrzNN, rrzNN[letter], or a full special
device name.
For most modern disk drives the total number of
sectors will not be equal to sectors * tracks * cylinders because of
variable drive geometry from inner cylinder to outer cylinder.
However, the number of tracks and sectors make a reasonable starting place
from which one can produce a disktab entry.
.SH CAVEATS
You have to be super-user to run
.B sizedrive.
