It is a modular communication server.  One of the cards offered is the
Network PRotocol Translator.  I can give you details on how it works but
basically you set up a LAT service.  Whenever anyone on the DECserver
does SHOW SERVICES they will see this service.  When They say Connect (foo)
the next thing they will see is the unix logon prompt.  

It also works in the other direction  (i.e. telnet to an ip address
or Domain name and the next thing you see is the vax prompt)

Advantages over host software based solutions:
* Easier to install.  I personally can set this service up in
under 5 minutes once the VCP1000 is out of the box.  No mucking about
installing software on the host.

* PRobably less expensive

* less overhead on host.  This approach requires no additional host overhead.
