ML-->>hi guys/gals,

ML-->>i'd like to know how to do multi volume backup from disk to tape.
-->>(effectively a full system backup)
-->>i'm using vms ver 5.0.

I've got a fairly good DCL routine written that I use nightly to back up
5 disks onto one 8MM.

It starts with inquiry screens asking you what disks you want to back
up, and what tapes you want to back up to (I have 2 8mm's and 1 TK50)
It asks if you want the backup to be verified, if you want to use the
/LIST option (to print out what got backed up) and if you want session
logging (Using 3rd party software)

It initializes and labels the tape(s) DDMMM with day/month of system
date, backs up the drives specified, keeping track of the times required
to back up each drive, and reports total time required to do the backup.

It then remounts the tape FILES-11 and does a directory/siz/date on the
tape to confirm that there are indeed 5 savesets there.

Lastly, it sends E-mail containing start times, completion times and
tape directory information to my system manager and myself to let us
know that the backup process complete.

I originally wrote this when we were running VMS 5.3 and rewrote when we
upgraded to 5.5-2H4 so there might be some stuff in it you would have to
change, but you're welcome to a listing of it.  It would be a bit
lengthy to post on the net, though.

