	That isn't an issue of Multiware, but the application server.  For
instance, the Microsoft Mail server does not run on Multiware using VAX or AXP. 
The Microsoft Mail server may make use of VAX or AXP disks, but still requires
its own server to actually run the server portion of the distributed
application. Like I said, while many OS's may support file and print servers,
once you get to client-server applications your choices start to get limited. 
That doesn't mean that the application server couldn't be made to work on a
different platform, such as with Multiware.  However, until the vendor
implements the application server on Multiware, you get to use yet another
server.

