   In article <Cn6uEJ.8n3@freenet.carleton.ca>, ae299@FreeNet.Carleton.CA (Michel Lee) writes:
> 
> 
> i'd like to know how to do multi volume backup from disk to tape.
> (effectively a full system backup)
> i'm using vms ver 5.0.
> assuming i have 3 diskdevices in my machine: (namely dka1:,dka2:,dka3:)
> and a tape device name mka1:
> 
> will it be this command?->
> 
> backup/image/ignore=(interlock,label_processing)/rewind     -
>     dka1:,dka2:,dka3:      mka1:myback.bck
> 
   There are two reasons you would not wish to issue the above command.

   First, it is invalid as you cannot have a list of devices for /IMAGE and
   there is no /SAVE_SET qualifier on the saveset.

   Second, (as if it matters :-) you would have all the data in a single
   saveset so should you need to restore a disk you would have a real pain to
   restore.

   I suggest doing the following command:

   $ BACKUP/IMAGE/IGNORE=(INTERLOCK,LABEL_PROCESSING)/VERIFY -
   	<dev>: MKA1:IMG<dev>.BCK/SAVE_SET

   Where you substitute the device name for <dev>.

   Note that in addition to adding the /SAVE_SET qualifier, I also added the
   /VERIFY qualifier.  This is a case of being paranoid but my view is the
   added time of reading the 'saved' data and being sure the tape is sane is
   worth it.  All it takes is one bad tape to ruin your whole day, especially
   if you don't discover it was bad until head crash day.

   Another minor nit is that using IGNORE LABEL_PROCESSING can bite you.  Using
   this means you are SURE you have the right volume mounted in the drive.

>  
> also what will happen if the tape gets full, will vms prompt me for
> new tapes? 
> 

   The BACKUP utility will prompt you and anyone with TAPE operator enabled on
   their terminal when it wishes another tape.  It expects the label to be the
   next tape label in sequence and if not you will be prompted as to whether
   you wish to Retry, Abort, or Overwrite the tape loaded as the next volume.

   There is extensive help for BACKUP.  Just do HELP BACKUP and you will
   receive a great deal of information including many examples.

   Have fun,
   don


