|>%LINK-E-MULSHRPSC, psect ERRNO defined in shareable image 
|>	SYS$COMMON:[SYSLIB]LGPSHR.EXE;5
|>
[more text omitted]

The linker is now complaining about an error it didn't notice before; that
two shareable images try to "define" the same GBL,OVR PSECT.  The two
images are LGPSHR and VAXCRTL.  It suggests that LGPSHR was linked against
the VAX C RTL objects rather than the shareable image, which is bad news,
but then if it was, and you had no C code in your application, how are you
pulling in VAXCRTL.EXE?

Do you have LNK$LIBRARY defined?  If so, as what?  Try adding the following
linker options file:

	SYS$LIBRARY:VAXCRTL/SHARE

and see what happens.

If that doesn't help, use the following options file instead:

	PSECT_ATTR=ERRNO,LCL
