In article <1994Mar21.202510.60788@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu>, 
mtovar@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes:
|>I am new to an organization that provides consulting to DEC clients.
|>I'm comfortable with IBM's AS/400, but am wanting to come up to speed
|>on the DEC Vax and Alpha series.  Can anybody recommend good books,
|>trade publications, or the like?

Digital operates an extensive archive service on the Internet which has
thousands of documents relating to Digital and its products.  Information
is available through FTP, WAIS and World-Wide-Web.  I recommend the WWW
interface; it's well indexed and keyword searching is available.

For WWW (Mosaic, Lynx, etc.) use URL http://www.dec.com/info.html
For WAIS and anonymous FTP use gatekeeper.dec.com

There are a number of trade publications which cover Digital's products,
such as Digital News and Review and Digital Systems Journal.  Digital has
some of its own publications which you can find out about from the
archive server.
