Hello,

I'm testing a DLT867. I had it from an o.e.m , not directly from DEC.
It looks very solid and I'm satisfied of the performance.
I'm satisifed also of the performance of the drive.
It can store 6GBytes on a cartridge and can access each file very fast.
there are several trackes (56?) and when I need to skip several files
the hard select the rigth track and then move on it until it finds the file.
the access time is 70 second on average  but  it takes from 20sec to 160sec
(file at the beginning and at the end of a track).

But...

sometimes the directory information get corrupted. So if I want to go to a
file in the middle of the tape must go forward on the first track, come back on
the second and so on until it finds the file. When the drive finds the file
position, it remember its position and the position off all the files it has
skipped on to arrive there.  Good...If the directory gets corrupted I can scan
all the tape up to the last file and rebuild all the information. it can take
a couple of hour but after that I can access each file in less that 160 seconds.

Unfortunately...

