Date: 18 Mar 1994 14:14:04 GMT
Lines: 144


A problem has been found with my adaptation of Clyde Hoover's
"npasswd" program for Ultrix running at the UPGRADE and ENHANCED
security levels.

Under certain circumstances, the program could leave /etc/passwd
locked from other accesses, resulting in a denial of service.  Since
/etc/passwd is not modified if the password is not stored there, there
is no reason to lock the file in the first place.

If you are running npasswd under Ultrix UPGRADE/ENHANCED security you
should either download a fresh copy of the code from
black.ox.ac.uk/src/security/npasswd_enhanced.shar.Z or you should
apply the patch below to the file pw_enhanced.c

My thanks to keppingm@ucs.orst.edu (Mark Keppinger) for identifying
this problem and for supplying the fix.

Paul

