financial reserves.

>Estimated VAX sales declined by 40% annualized.

Like, suprise me.  For those who haven't been paying attention,
VAX computers are on the way out.  DEC's flagship platform for VMS is
now the AXP (sales of which are booming, naturally).

>Revenue dropped 12 % for the quarter to US$ 3.3 billion 

Unlike everything else you quote, this *is* a worrying statistic, but
a more relevant statistic to DEC's relative health would be market
share.

> DEC's only profitable quarter since March 1991 was US$ 113.2 million in the 
