>
>DEC's 1992 ficscal year losses were US$ 2.8 billion.
>
>Some of you might see this a signs of health, but I'm not ready to invest.

Like IBM, DEC took some big losses due to restructuring to cost cut
costs.  This is not a worry of itself: they can afford it, and it
improves their future prospects for profitability.   This is not to
imply that I am ready to invest either, but remember that most
investors are interested in long term trends, and in this context DEC
and IBM's problems are (so far) only blips on the normal economic
cycles.



