There are a lot of variables to take into account and several ways your system
could be configured to accomplish this.  On our ALL-IN-FUN system, we can
address internet mail as:

	"longo@sfpp.com" @uucp 
or	"longo@sfpp.com" @internet
or	"longo@sfpp.com" @ uucp @ mrgate
or	_"uucp""longo@sfpp.com""

Some of these work because we have a system logical name "UUCP" which is
defined as "node::uucp%" (where 'node' is the node running the UUCP software)
and others work because our message router has the following relacements
established:

	UUCP,                     Replace=@UUCP@MRGATE
and	INTERNET,                 Replace=@UUCP@MRGATE

As for SMTP - sorry, can't help you there.  We don't use it.

Good luck,
