Stan Swiercz (stan@cs.concordia.ca) wrote:
: We have a brand new DEC 3000/400 and one of the professors would like
: to attach a modem to it so that he can call in from home. I have tried 
: various things with no positive results. We're a Sun shop and this is our
: first DEC machine running OSF.

: I've checked the manual we received and looked in the FAQ. Could some 
: kind soul provide me with a short step by step description of what
: I have to do to get the modem to answer the phone and issue a login
: prompt from the alpha.

I've connected two modems to a DECserver 700 (DS700) which is what you
also have to do. OR, at least you need a (full?) modem control port.

I took the following steps.
'Standard' Hayes AT-commands used...consult your modem manual as the 
commands may vary depending on manufacturer. I used two GVC FM-144 modems.

1. Configure the modem as follows :
	- autoanswer (S0=1)
	- FIXED DTE speed (\J0)
	- bidirectional hardware flow control (\Q3)
	- most flexible answer mode (usually B0 or B1)
	- hang up, return to command mode after DTR toggle (&D2)
	- turn on Carrier Detect when remote carrier is present (&C1)
	- modem does not send responses (Q1)
	- compression, error control etc. enabled but adjusts link according
	  to originating modem.

	Also you have to set the modems DTE speed to the port's speed.
	This has often to be done with bitmap register S23. Consult your
	modem manual.

	- save configuartion in non-volatile memory (&W) and check that
	  profile 0 will be the default active profile.
	PS. IT IS VITAL FOR THE DTE-SPEED-SETTING TO BE SET WITH THE LAST 
	    SAVE AS YOUR MODEM SET THE DTE-SPEED AFTER EVERY AT-COMMAND.
	    i.e. last command would be ATS23=xx&W  , xx=decimal value
	    for DTE-speed-setting.

2. Configure the port as follows:
	- flow control CTS
	- Input- and output speed as for the modem DTE-speed
	- modem control enabled
	- autobaud disabled
	- input/output flow control, DTRwait all enabled
	- character size parity etc. according to modem settings.

These setting are, asI pointed out earlier, for a DEC DS700 terminal server
and a GVC FM-144 modem(faxmodem).

If possible, check the answering modem with e.g. two PC's including a terminal
program.

I hope I didn't leave out anything vital. If you have further problems,
I'm reachable at e-mail ahlstedt@mits.mdata.fi

--JA--



