 kind of a special fondness/attachment for the *first* thing/person that you
 had/did/learned/operated/loved ?  It must be the "mother tongue" syndrome.
 Those experiences and feelings get written in our brains at a very low level
 and we use these thought patterns forever more to measure and judge other
 things/people who may be in that same "facet".  So, those that grew up on 
 unix will always love unix and will judge the world by its standards, and
 those who were weaned on Messy-dos will always love Messy-dos, as a rule.
