Then there's the behavior known as "satisficing."  Faced with a choice between
many alternatives, most people will tend to evaluate the first few in a fair
amount of detail, and not invest much time or effort in evaluating alternatives
presented to them later, sticking with the "best so far" unless a new
alternative is obviously, on cursory inspection, significantly better than the
previous alternatives.
