The U.S. Chapter of DECUS, the Digital Equipment Computer Users Society, 
today announced major enhancements to its Internet-based Information Server, 
making a variety of information on the organization readily available to an 
estimated audience of over 10 million users. 

The DECUS Information Server was established in the Fall of 1993 as an 
electronic outlet for posting information on DECUS symposium events. Recent 
enhancements, implemented in time for the upcoming DECUS '94/New Orleans 
event scheduled for May 7-12, 1994, make it easier for users to access 
information on seminar and symposium offerings.

Since its inception, the number and variety of files posted on the 
