the structure of the Chapter; the DECUS Software Library; DECUServe, the 
Chapter's electronic conferencing system; and Digital Equipment Corporation, 
as well as copies of technical publications; archive materials; and other 
supporting documents on Chapter activities.

The list of tools for accessing the Information Server have also grown to 
include: Anonymous FTP; Mailserv; and most recently, a user-friendly Gopher 
server.

The DECUS Gopher server allows users to browse and retrieve information 
through a series of easy to use menu options. The server also provides a 
keyword search facility for selected files including those which contain 
abstracts of seminar and symposium sessions of DECUS '94/New Orleans. Users 
can review seminar and symposium session offerings by topic, speaker, date, 
or any other number of criteria through the keyword facility.

A full listing of seminar titles and abstracts, and symposium session titles 
are now available for review on the Gopher server. A file containing all 
symposium session abstracts is expected to be added to the server the week 
of March 21, 1994.

