>
>I had to discover for myself how to
>resume a process when I typed ctrl/z in it (which is a habit from my
>VMS days I found hard to break).  

Yeah, I got tired of that too.  Easy to fix:

stty susp ^D
stty eof ^Z
stty quit ^Y

Put in .login if you are using csh or tcsh.  This swaps the meaning of
CTRL/D and CTRL/Z, and you get a free CTRL/Y as well.  So now you can
use CTRL/Z as ususal.  But don't get confused with docs now.

Michael
