	What I'm asking is what if you are writing an application, what
if you want to arrange the arguments differents rather than have all the
file names at the very end of the command line?  As to what purpose, that's
the programmers decision, and shouldn't be forced because of the nature of
what the shell is going to do.  For example:

	$ SEARCH *.* STRING

	I decide I like a "grep" like organization, so I change the command
definition (but no code) to get:

	$ GREP STRING *.*

	Because of the modular separation of DCL, CLD, and the program,
you can arrange your arguments and qualifiers however you decide.  Even
change your mind without impacting the code.

