Carl J Lydick:
	   % grep * file.name

* isn't a valid search string for grep, even if it were quoted.  * is
a meta character such that x* represents 0 or more occurences of x.  x
may be a single character, a set of characters, a string, a set of
strings, or some other arbitrary regular expression.

As far as I know, 
   grep '*' files
will just search for a literal asterisk, but even that is rather bad
form.  I'd probably use
  fgrep '*' files

fgrep deals with fixed strings, rather than regular expressions.

Raul D. Miller
<rockwell@nova.umd.edu>


