Marginally.  I might point out that, generally, the VMS case would
be "$ show users".  Very few people do everything entirely in upper case.
While it is true that VMS stores and presents a lot of stuff in uppercase,
usernames, symbols, and node names for example, input in lower or mixed case
works just fine and very few people keep their terminal in caps-lock mode.
The same goes for all the following examples, of course.

}Now look at Joe Sixpack,
}
}sixpack: "Ok, I want to see what my files are."
}
}$ SHOW FILES
}
}"nope"
}
}$ TYPE FILES
}
}"uh uh."
}
}$ DISPLAY NAMES/FILE
}
}"Aw comeon".
}
}$ LIST FILENAMES
}
}dammit.
}
}$ *.*/DISPLAY
}
}argh.
}
