proprietary O/S is that one company owns it, and thus defines what happens
to it, and how quickly the "what happens" happens. Take MS-Windows/DOS, 
this is a company with a huge monopoly they control the market, they decide
what innovation customers get and when they get it.

Ideally what we want is to encourage innovation, prevent duplication of
effort and to allow cusotmers access to new technology.

Customers don't want to be tied into a particular hardware platfrom  and
want to be free to make choices whenever possible.

