Ok, you don't want to, but others may.  The advantage of support of
various file types, is that any application programmer can process the
file without having to know anything about it -- or even know what type
of file will be used at run-time.  For example, a program can be written
that sequentially processes a file -- at runtime a sequential file, or an
indexed or relative file can be processed.  Under UNIX the programmer
would need to know that an indexed file will be used and make use of that
software directly, putting the entire burden of managing these situations
on the application programmer.  In addition, if I buy third party
software, I know it will work with RMS.

