I like the idea that an application doesn't really need to know that it
is reading from (or writting to) a tape instead of disk.  We receive a
lot of information from other companies on tape (asI'm sure many other
commercial shops do).  We also get data across the net as disk files.
It's nice that the program doesn't care which (without the added step of
loading it to disk first, then deleting the disk version after).  In
addition, some of the tape files are very large and we are only
interested in a subset of the records, why bring the entire file to disk
first?




