    in industry.



2) Digital is about to complete the transition started over two years ago
   with restructuring charges, new business units, and the rollout of 
   Alpha.   
    Digital is poised to begin making money again.

3) The industry is focusing more and more on Client/Server to implement 
   solutions.  Today Digital has a clear lead in "Integrated" Client/Server
   middleware that makes this implementation possible.  Just having the 
   standards isn't enough, customers need to see interoperablity "Out of 
   the Box". Digital's NAS softwares are uniquely positioned to do just 
   that.



> Estimated VAX sales declined by 40% annualized.
