Actually the number of License sold and the Total number of OpenVMS
users have never been higher.  The 40% decline is really due to lower
hardware and software margins per unit then just two years ago.

OpenVMS/AXP sales are increasing, OpenVMS sales are increasing too, the 
real culpret behind the declining revenue is lower prices and faster 
boxes.  Customers are finding that they can downsize their VAX 65xx 
into a 4xxx with no appriciable performance difference at a much lower
cost in licenses, peripherals and maintenance.

If their software is available on AXP systems they can take advantage of 
even greater price/performance, lowering even more the margins Digital 
used to make for a 'GIVEN' amount of compute power.



