In article <CMDuBt.CsG@world.std.com> jcomeau@world.std.com (John O Comeau) writes:
>Rick Dyson (dyson@iowasp.physics.uiowa.edu) wrote:
>: I am looking for some information about suppressing extra blank pages on
>: HP LaserJet printers connected to VAX/VMS print queues.  I am using
>: VAX/VMS v5.5-1 and a HP LaserJet IIID.  Any info on a FAQ, etc. would be
>: greatly appreciated.

I ran into the same problem you did with the extra pages on a HP III printer
on a VMS queue.  I have all of my HPIII printers connected to some DECserver
of some sort or another.  Check out the VMS manual Guide to Maintaining a 
VMS System.  Look in Chapter 5, Using Device Control Library Modules.  I
set up a text library like this:

	$ LIBRARY/CREATE/TEXT SYS$LIBRARY:HPDEVCTL.TLB

The book explains it pretty well.  Anyway, I created a reset module called
HP_RESET.TXT  Then I inserted it into the library.  In the book, Example
5.1 shows exactly how to do this.  The escape sequences I used in the reset
module were:

	<ESC>]VMS;2<ESC>\<ESC>P<ESC>E<ESC>\

Then, make sure your printer queue has a /SEPARATE=RESET=HP_RESET and
a /LIBRARY=HPDEVCTL qualifier on it.  If this doesn't work for you, you
can give me a call or mail me at OGAWA@WHMC-LAFB.AF.MIL 
Don't sent to the account I've posted from here, this is my school account.

Scott Ogawa




