want it to.  You don't need a special driver, just install it
as a generic printer with the following STTYPARAMS 

STTYPARAMS="-ixany ixon ixoff -opost"

We use "ghostscript" from GNU (have you heard of ghostview which uses gs to 
provide an excellent postscript previewer?).  We currently have gs262 
installed.  gs allows you to read in a postscript file and convert it to 
quite a large number of different formats, including Deskjet.  It's available 
via anonymous ftp from numerous sites (e.g. gatekeeper.dec.com in directory
/contrib/share/lib/ghostscript) and is relatively easy to build!  The best
thing about it is that is not only an excellent product, but it is also free!

