> are orders of magnitude bigger than older ``monoltical'' kernels.
> Spring OS, as far as I can tell, not a product, not is it meant to be,
> at this time.
> 
Spring OS is currently in development and is designed in the future
to be the next OS after Solaris for SUN.
But, Workplace OS from IBM that is definitely launching this year
is a microkerel. It uses Mach 3 (I believe) which does
not have the monolithic parts of Unix that earlier Mach's possesed. 
Even Apple is apparently microkerneling system 7.


