In article <ROCKWELL.94Mar4221202@nova.umd.edu>, rockwell@nova.umd.edu (Raul Deluth Miller) writes:
=One more question: how do I get these commands to present this
=information to me a screen at a time?

There are a number of ways of doing it.  You could create a subprocess using
TYPE/PAGE and feed the output of your command to a mailbox from which the
subprocess is typing.  Or you could put code in your procedure to handle the
pagination.

=Or do I have to do that in my
=terminal emulator?  [Can be tricky with ordinary terminal emulator on
=a high speed connection.]

Here's an example of putting the code in the procedure.  

$	IF	F$GETDVI("SYS$OUTPUT", "TRM")
$	THEN	NLINES = F$GETDVI("SYS$OUTPUT", "TT_PAGE") - 1
$	ELSE	NLINES = 0
$	ENDIF
$	N = 0
$ LOOP:	DEV = F$DEVICE("*")
$	IF DEV .EQS. "" THEN EXIT
$	WRITE SYS$OUTPUT DEV
$	IF NLINES .EQ. 0 THEN GOTO LOOP
$	N = N + 1
$	IF	N .GE. NLINES
$	THEN	READ/PROMPT="Hit return to continue" SYS$COMMAND FUBAR
$		N = 0
$	ENDIF
$	GOTO LOOP

