The GIGAswitch System: A High-Performance Packet Switching Platform

	The GIGAswitch(tm) System is a very high-performance packet-
	switching platform built on a 36-port 100 Mbit/second crossbar
	switching fabric capable of 6.25 million connections/second.
	The GIGAswitch System platform is data link independent.
	The first GIGAswitch System product offering uses 2-port FDDI
	line cards to construct a 22-port IEEE 802.1d FDDI bridge.
	A 4-port FDDI line card is under development, as is a
	multifunction 2-port line card providing SONET STS-3c
	(155 Mbits/sec), T3 (45 Mbits/sec) and/or E3 (34 Mbits/sec)
	using ATM.  Distributed forwarding, in hardware, yields
	forwarding rates greater than 200,000 packets per second per
	port.  In this paper, we present an overview of the switch
	architecture and discuss the principles influencing its design.
	We then describe the implementation of an FDDI bridge on the
	GIGAswitch System platform and conclude with the results of
	performance measurements made during system test.

To appear in Digital Technical Journal, vol. 6 no. 1 (1994), 18 pages.
GIGAswitch is a trademark of Digital Equipment Corporation.


