	rockwell@nova.umd.edu wrote:

	> =One more question?  How do I get a list of all disks?


	To which Carl Lydick replied:

	>         $ SHOW DEV D
	> if you just want a list of the disks that are mounted:
	>         $ SHOW DEV D/MOUNTED

Correct, but not complete.  "SHOW DEV D" shows most (all?) physical
disks (and some virtual disks, such as shadow sets), but does not pick
up stripe set virtual disks.  To see stripe sets, one should use "SHOW
DEV ST" in addition to "SHOW DEV D".  (There may also be other types
of virtual disks with which I am not familiar, and for which one might
need an additional "SHOW DEV x" command.  For example, does anybody
know how RAID disks are named?)
