Furthermore, VAX FORTRAN will automatically determine the logical record length
for an existing file on open, if it's a fixed-record-length file (i.e., you
don't have to specify RECL in the OPEN statement), and if you want to access it
sequentially, that's the default.  Now, when you try to read a record in the
file, and you specify more data elements than the amount of data in the record
can accomodate, you'll get an error.  That, however, is true for ANY valid
FORTRAN implementation.  It's only when you want to take advantage of
additional features offered by RMS that you've got to take special steps in
OPENing the file.  Once again, Bruce whines that if he wants to do more with
