My perspective is that rather than have the OS try to provide every way of 
structuring my access to files IT can think of, and then miss the one way I 
want to do it, I'd rather have the OS provide a simple, fast mechanism over 
which I can implement servers to implement other abstractions.  If the OS 
developers then exert their efforts to make sure that IPC to those servers 
is fast and efficient, then I can implement exactly what I need and have it 
perform better than a generic service the OS provides.

Does VMS provide Informix or Oracle file access semantics?  SQL?  If that's 
the access mode my apps need, then the efforts VMS has made to provide 
other services have only increased the size of the OS, and perhaps the 
added complexity has created other tradeoffs not beneficial to my 
applications.
