Yes, the VMS HELP utility does that.  No, the VMS help utility doesn't, by
default, access all the help libraries on the system.  They're accessed by the
individual programs (e.g., SYS$HELP:MAILHELP.HLB is accessed by the VMS MAIL
utility).  Those individual programs use LBR$OUTPUT_HELP, which does not, by
default, do any paging (it uses LIB$PUT_OUTPUT for output, and LIB$PUT_OUTPUT
does NOT do paging).

Furthermore, Raul was asking how you get a generic command (not necessarily one
outputting help information) to do pagination.
