Try the following script on your Unix box under any shell you wish.  It
fails for me under SunOS 4.1.x, SunOS 5.3, Irix 4.0.5, and Ultrix 4.3a.
I've tried sh, ksh (both vendor supplied and PD), and csh. (btw. SunOS 5.x
no longer supplies the yes command).

#!/bin/sh
for I in `yes | cat -n | tr -d y | head -400`; do
    touch file.${I}.a file.${I}.b file.${I}.c file.${I}.d file.${I}.e
done
chmod 755 *

Doug

PS. I would run this in an *empty* directory. :)
