Not without an argument it won't.  For example, SHOW DEVICE without an argument
won't show any mailbox devices.  To get a list of all devices:
	$ LOOP:	DEV = F$DEVICE("*")
	$	IF DEV .EQS. "" THEN EXIT
	$	WRITE SYS$OUTPUT DEV
	$	GOTO LOOP

=Show device with no argument gives you everybody, which on everything but
=single-user desktop systems could be a rather substantial list (but most
=DCL things can send their output to a file with the /output= qualifier).

Again, it doesn't show you mailboxes.
