> unix systems have been more pleasant to use [you can have a larger
> storage quota, you can run more processes, etc...].

	The question was "How can DEC make VMS more attractive to Univ's".
By providing cheap hardware and software resources, this would make it
very attractive to them.

	And again the "larger storage, more processes" has nothing to do
with the O/S, but with the PEOPLE running the system.

>    >>  8. How can DEC make VMS attractive to software developers?
>    > Shells.
> 
