A problem with the ZLX-M2 manifests itself on some machines when it is 
connected to a VRT19-HA monitor. If the X server restarts for any reason
(-terminate, terminateServer: true, server crash ;^( ) on some machines, the
cursor will be off about 40 pixels in the X and 20 pixels in the Y direction.
This affects the "console" cursor as well (init s). The server works fine on 
the first go-around - it's only second & subsequent startups. 
The cause is currently unknown but the workaround is easy - change the jumper 
on the ZLX from 66 to 72 Hz.

The HA's I have are auto-syncing - why such bizzare behaviour is beyond me.
DEC Graphics has be appraised of the problem & workaround - I'm sure a fix'll
be out soon.

